From ab2964b85b21327030b76ef3851a1bb72b4c5381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashesh Vidyut <asheshvidyut@google.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 15:21:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Pin Python test binds and dials to 127.0.0.1 across the
 test tree

Soak testing (repeating the 16x flake qualification run) kept catching
the same failure class one file at a time: a test binds [::]:0 or
localhost and dials localhost, and the client resolves localhost to
both loopback addresses. A foreign listener holding the specific
127.0.0.1 twin of the port (another concurrently running test, or an
unrelated local process; observed with a Docker-forwarded port that
answers HTTP/2 404) beats the test's wildcard listener for IPv4
traffic or captures the fallback path, yielding UNIMPLEMENTED from
strangers, writes failing mid-stream, and hangs.

Mechanically pin bind and dial to 127.0.0.1 across the remaining
test files. Excluded: TLS tests whose certificates are bound to the
localhost hostname, and DNS resolver tests that dial hostnames on
purpose (bind-only pinning there). channel_argument_test's reuseport
probe is pinned to the address the server binds so it keeps
contending for the same socket.
